x86\\avx512f.rs","begin":[7936,1],"end":[7949,2]},"visibility":"public","docs":"Subtract packed double-precision (64-bit) floating-point elements in b from packed double-precision (64-bit) floating-point elements in a, and store the results in dst using writemask k (elements are copied from src when the corresponding mask bit is not set).\\\n\nRounding is done according to the rounding\\[3:0\\] parameter, which can be one of:\\\n* [`_MM_FROUND_TO_NEAREST_INT`] | [`_MM_FROUND_NO_EXC`] : round to nearest and suppress exceptions\n* [`_MM_FROUND_TO_NEG_INF`] | [`_MM_FROUND_NO_EXC`] : round down and suppress exceptions\n* [`_MM_FROUND_TO_POS_INF`] | [`_MM_FROUND_NO_EXC`] : round up and suppress exceptions\n* [`_MM_FROUND_TO_ZERO`] | [`_MM_FROUND_NO_EXC`] : truncate and suppress exceptions\n* [`_MM_FROUND_CUR_DIRECTION`] : use `MXCSR.RC` - see [`_MM_SET_ROUNDING_MODE`]\n\n[Intel's documentation](https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/docs/intrinsics-guide/index.html#text=_mm512_mask_sub_round_pd&expand=5734)","links":{"`_MM_FROUND_TO_POS_INF`":35081,"`_MM_SET_ROUNDING_MODE`":34821,"`_MM_FROUND_TO_NEAREST_INT`":35079,"`_MM_FROUND_NO_EXC`":35085,"`_MM_FROUND_TO_NEG_INF`":35080,"`_MM_FROUND_TO_ZERO`":35082,"`_MM_FROUND_CUR_DIRECTION`":35083},"attrs":[{"other":"#[<cfg_attr>(test, assert_instr(vsubpd, ROUNDING = 8))]"},{"other":"#[rustc_legacy_const_generics(4)]"},{"other":"#[attr = Stability {stability: Stability {level: Stable {since: Version(RustcVersion {major: 1,\nminor: 89, patch: 0})}, feature: \"stdarch_x86_avx512\"}}]"},{"target_feature":{"enable":["avx512f"]}},{"other":"#[attr = Inline(Hint)]"}],"deprecation":null,"inner":{"function":{"sig":{"inputs":[["src",{"resolved_path":{"path":"__m512d","id":9295,"args":null}}],["k",{"resolved_path":{"path":"__mmask8","id":35711,"args":null}}],["a",{"resolved_path":{"path":"__m512d","id":9295,"args":null}}],["b",{"resolved_path":{"path":"__m512d","id":9295,"args":null}}],["ROUNDING",{"primitive":"i32"}]],"output":{"resolved_pa