XCSR.RC` - see [`_MM_SET_ROUNDING_MODE`]\n\n[Intel's documentation](https://software.intel.com/sites/landingpage/IntrinsicsGuide/#text=_mm256_maskz_roundscale_ph)","links":{"`_MM_FROUND_TO_POS_INF`":35081,"`_MM_SET_ROUNDING_MODE`":34821,"`_MM_FROUND_TO_NEAREST_INT`":35079,"`_MM_FROUND_CUR_DIRECTION`":35083,"`_MM_FROUND_TO_NEG_INF`":35080,"`_MM_FROUND_TO_ZERO`":35082},"attrs":[{"other":"#[<cfg_attr>(test, assert_instr(vrndscaleph, IMM8 = 0))]"},{"other":"#[rustc_legacy_const_generics(2)]"},{"other":"#[attr = Stability {stability: Stability {level: Unstable {reason: None,\nissue: 127213, is_soft: false}, feature: \"stdarch_x86_avx512_f16\"}}]"},{"target_feature":{"enable":["avx512fp16","avx512vl"]}},{"other":"#[attr = Inline(Hint)]"}],"deprecation":null,"inner":{"function":{"sig":{"inputs":[["k",{"resolved_path":{"path":"__mmask16","id":35708,"args":null}}],["a",{"resolved_path":{"path":"__m256h","id":9310,"args":null}}],["IMM8",{"primitive":"i32"}]],"output":{"resolved_path":{"path":"__m256h","id":9310,"args":null}},"is_c_variadic":false},"generics":{"params":[],"where_predicates":[]},"header":{"is_const":false,"is_unsafe":false,"is_async":false,"abi":"Rust"},"has_body":true}}},"1089":{"id":1089,"crate_id":0,"name":"overflowing_neg","span":{"filename":"library\\core\\src\\num\\mod.rs","begin":[247,5],"end":[266,6]},"visibility":"public","docs":"Negates self, overflowing if this is equal to the minimum value.\n\nReturns a tuple of the negated version of self along with a boolean indicating whether an overflow\nhappened. If `self` is the minimum value (e.g., `i32::MIN` for values of type `i32`), then the\nminimum value will be returned again and `true` will be returned for an overflow happening.\n\n# Examples\n\n```\nassert_eq!(2i8.overflowing_neg(), (-2, false));\nassert_eq!(i8::MIN.overflowing_neg(), (i8::MIN, true));\n```","links":{},"attrs":[{"other":"#[allow(unused_attributes)]"},{"other":"#[attr = ConstStability {stability: PartialConstStability {level: Stable {s